**1. Terminal Operations**  
The terminal at Port of San Diego has maintained a steady flow of operations this past week. As of March 9, we handled a total of 1,200 TEUs (Twenty-foot Equivalent Units), which marks a 15% increase compared to the previous week. The increase can be attributed to the recent collaboration with Global Trade Partners (GTP), which has streamlined our cargo handling procedures.  

**2. Cargo Handling**  
The cargo handling team, led by Maria Chen, has implemented an upgraded tracking system using RFID technology. This system has reduced misplacement incidents by 30% and improved the overall efficiency of loading and unloading. For example, we successfully completed a turnaround time of 2.5 hours for the Maersk Alabama, which arrived on March 8.  

**3. Customs Processes**  
Our customs clearance process remains critical to ensuring that all cargo is compliant with both domestic and international regulations. As of now, we have successfully cleared 95% of our incoming shipments through the Automated Commercial Environment (ACE) system. I want to remind everyone that accurate documentation is paramount. In the last week, we faced delays for two containers due to incomplete paperwork. Maria, please ensure that your team double-checks all documentation before submission to prevent recurrence.  

**4. Vessel Scheduling**  
